# Live data & secrets — never commit (see CLAUDE.md)
*.db
*.db.*
*.secret
*.env
*.token
ingest.env
# Operational detail and clinical term lists stay on the machine.
# THIS REPOSITORY IS PUBLIC - see tools/NO_SECRETS.py
*.local.txt
*.local.md
*.local.json
# WhatsApp invite texts name family members (getting_started_sheet.py --kitchen)
fitlog-ingest/Kitchen_invite_messages*.txt
*.log
*.bak
*.bak-*
*.bak_*
# patch_fitlog_ist_and_steps.py and patch_workout_day_ist.py stamp their
# rollback copies '.bak.<stamp>'. Neither pattern above matches that
# spelling, and neither does the findstr gate in PUBLISH_HEALTH.bat, so a
# .bak of a sensitive file would have been committed to a PUBLIC repo.
*.bak.*
*.deployed-*
# a patcher's half-written copy of the file it was patching, if os.replace
# never ran. Same hazard class as a .bak.
*.tmp
# The briefs that commission this work quote the record they are about:
# molecule names, dates, findings. They are working notes, not deliverables,
# and THIS REPOSITORY IS PUBLIC. 2026-09-14: the Phase J brief named two
# molecules and a Holter result, and `git add -A` would have taken it.
# NOTE: CLAUDE_CODE_PROMPT_pain_v1.md and _fitlog.md were committed before
# this rule existed. Ignoring a path does not untrack it, so for weeks this
# rule sat here doing nothing while the files stayed in the tree. pain_v1.md
# is now untracked AND purged from every commit; _fitlog.md names no medicine
# or condition and is kept by decision. See the CHANGELOG for 2026-09-14.
fitlog-ingest/CLAUDE_CODE_PROMPT_*.md
# Same class: a planning document that named a molecule and a drug class he
# takes. Untracked and purged from history on 2026-09-14.
rxguard/PLAN_MedKnowledge_v1.md

# Runtime junk
__pycache__/
*.pyc
venv/
uploads/
nohup.out

# RxGuard source-sync cache and lock (downloaded public data, rebuilt on the server)
knowledge/cache/
.kb_sync.lock

# Local deploy bundles (copies of files that live in the app folders)
_deploy/

# scan_lab working files: synthetic photographs and their measurements are
# regenerated by make_images.py, not carried in the repository.
gutlog/scan_lab/*.bin
gutlog/scan_lab/*.npy
gutlog/scan_lab/*.png
gutlog/scan_lab/*.json

# negative-control scratch builds (tools/NEGATIVE_CONTROL.py writes these beside app.py)
gutlog/_nc_*.py
*/_nc_*.py
_nc_mod_*/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2026-09-15. IMAGES AND OTHER BINARIES.
#
# Fifteen PNGs were tracked here and nine were pictures of the health record:
# the regimen with Indian brand names and strengths, stock counts, dated dose
# times, and two separate windows of blood pressure. Every NO_SECRETS run
# reported clean and was right to - A, B and C read TEXT, and a PNG is bytes.
# All nine came from gutlog/test_ui_now.py writing screenshots into the app
# folder, on every run, where `git add -A` collected them.
#
# THESE LINES ARE THE BACKSTOP, NOT THE REMEDY. `git add -f`, an edit to this
# file, or the next suite somebody writes all defeat them. The remedy is that
# test_ui_now.py now writes its screenshots OUTSIDE the repository entirely
# (GUTLOG_UI_SHOTS, refused if it points back inside) and asserts at the end
# of every run that it wrote no image into the tree. The second layer is
# NO_SECRETS check D, which refuses ANY tracked binary outside its two-icon
# allowlist - including a PNG renamed .md.
gutlog/*.png
!gutlog/icon-192.png
!gutlog/icon-512.png
Claude outputs/
fitlog-ingest/files.zip

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2026-09-22. PLAN AND REPORT DOCUMENTS.
#
# A plan PDF for GutLog's /plans page arrived in fitlog-ingest/ and was
# NEITHER tracked NOR ignored, so `git add -A` in PUBLISH_HEALTH.bat would
# have staged it. Its FILENAME alone named a medicine.
#
# It would have been refused - NO_SECRETS check D blocks any tracked binary
# outside the two-icon allowlist, and it was measured doing exactly that
# before this line was written. But note WHICH check caught it: the clinical
# checks B and C both reported clean, because they read text and a PDF is
# bytes. They never look at a filename. D was the only thing standing there.
#
# Per CLAUDE.md 5d the documents live on the server (/root/gutlog/plans_files/)
# and in the owner's PC folder. Never here.
*.pdf

